WB Questionnaire Designer
SPC assisted during the initial stages of designing the questionnaire with the Tonga
template used during the training they conducted.  The design for the Fiji Census
questionnaire was a lot less challenging as the questionnaire designer for survey
solutions was user friendly and other questionnaires available on-line for reference. The
designer used a structural design that allows for easy flow and capture of information
and with the use of rosters (even rosters within rosters), sections and subsections.
During the enumeration week Administrators and IT officers had to assign users for the
Enumerators, Supervisors and Headquarters staff.

--- page 51 ----------------------------------------------------
2017 Population and Housing Census, Administrative Report, 2018
Page 38
The 2017 Census questionnaire adopted the SPC Model which had eight modules with
Non Private Dwellings as the ninth. With a standard approach in mind via Census
questions across the region, the questions were modified to suit the Fiji context. The
Australian Bureau of Statistics also provided technical assistance in the whole
questionnaire design process.
SDG’s
FBoS officers attended both international and local workshops, consultations and
trainings and this proved to be useful guidance the collection of information that could
be used to provide benchmark information on a number of Sustainable Development
Goals indicators with the sustainable.
Figure 15: Sustainable Development Goals (SDG)
FBoS officers through invites attended both international and local workshops,
consultations and trainings so as to equip as much as providing resources on how
Census can be used to provide benchmark information on various indicators   to in line
with the sustainable goals.  This immensely helped in guiding the design of the Census
questionnaire.

